# qmldir — explicit module manifest for quickshell/modules/osd/ (Phase 20
# Plan 04, QOSD-01/QOSD-03; Plan 05, QOSD-02/QOSD-04). Mirrors every
# sibling module manifest's own standing instruction: any .qml type added
# to this directory that is NOT declared below becomes unresolvable to
# `shell.qml`'s `import "modules/osd"`. Any FUTURE type added to this
# directory MUST do the same, in the same commit that creates it.
#
# Osd is NOT a singleton — shell.qml mounts one ordinary, always-on
# instance (Toast.qml's own always-mounted posture, matching the DND
# toast), never behind a LazyLoader: the OSD must react to a volume/
# brightness/caps-lock change at any moment for the whole session, not
# only while some other surface is open.
#
# OsdSliderRow (Plan 05, QOSD-04) — the reusable slider row Osd.qml
# instantiates up to three times. CapsLockBackend (Plan 05, QOSD-02) — the
# glob-resolved, read-only, poll-driven Caps Lock detector Osd.qml mounts
# once (see that file's own header for why it is polled rather than
# watched). Neither is a singleton — Osd.qml owns exactly one instance of
# each.
module qs.modules.osd
Osd 1.0 Osd.qml
OsdSliderRow 1.0 OsdSliderRow.qml
CapsLockBackend 1.0 CapsLockBackend.qml
